  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Given that $z=-1-7\\text{i}$, calculate $z\\overset{\u2015}{z}.$",
  "worked_solution": "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we multiply a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always the sum of squares of the real part and the imaginary part.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=-1-7\\text{i},$ the real part is $\\text{Re}(z)=-1,$ and the imaginary part is $\\text{Im}(z)=-7,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{\u2015}{z} & =(\\text{Re}(z))^{2}+(\\text{Im}(z))^{2} \\\\  & =(-1)^{2}+(-7)^{2} \\\\  & =1+49 \\\\  & =50.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of multiplying the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=-1-7\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{\u2015}{z}=-1+7\\text{i}.$\n\nMultiplying, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{\u2015}{z} & =(-1-7\\text{i})(-1+7\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(-1)^{2}+(-1)(7)\\text{i}+(-7)(-1)\\text{i}-{\\text{i}}^{2}(7)^{2} \\\\  & =1-7\\text{i}+7\\text{i}-(-1)(49) \\\\  & =1+49 \\\\  & =50.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
